   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to naming a portion of route 202\nin the town of Yorktown the \"Captain Kenneth Sgroi Memorial Highway\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S5541",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5541-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-o, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5541\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to naming a portion of\nroute 202 in the town of Yorktown the \"Captain Kenneth Sgroi Memorial\nHighway\"\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo rename a portion of route 202 in the town of Yorktown in honor of\nPolice Captain Kenneth Sgroi who tragically passed away on January 2,\n2022\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 - Amends Highway law by adding a new section 344-o. Portion of\nthe state highway system to be designated as the \"Captain Kenneth Sgroi\nMemorial Highway.\"\n\nSection 2 - The Commissioner of Transportation shall provide for the\ninstallation and maintenance of adequate signage of the state highway\nsystem as designated pursuant to section one of this act. However, to\navoid confusion and to limit any possible disruption of commerce, the\ndesignation called for pursuant to section one of this act shall be one\nof ceremonial nature and the official name of such highway shall not be\nchanged as a result of this act.\n\nSection 3 - Effective date - Immediately\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCaptain Kenneth Sgroi of Yorktown Heights, New York, died on Monday,\nJanuary 2, 2023, at the age of 37. Captain Sgroi distinguished himself\nin his profession and by his sincere dedication and substantial contrib-\nution to the welfare of his community, his commitment to excellence, and\nhis spirit of humanity, carried over into all fields of enterprise,\nincluding charitable and civic endeavors.\n\nAs a patrol officer with the Yorktown Police Department (YPD), Kenneth\nSgroi was the first-place recipient of the Stop DWI award for the Town\nof Yorktown in 2010 and 2012; in 2013, he received a certificate of\ncommendation for his excellent work at the YPD, and he also became a\ncertified field training officer and a desk officer.In 2016, Kenneth\nSgroi was promoted to the rank of Sergeant and was assigned a patrol\nsquad to supervise as a Patrol Supervisor; he also oversaw the Yorktown\nPolice Department Field Training Program, and was promoted to the rank\nof Lieutenant in July of 2022, where he was assigned as the Staff Divi-\nsion Commander. In commendation of his dedication, hard work, and excel-\nlence throughout his tenure with the Yorktown Police Department, Lieu-\ntenant Sgroi was posthumously promoted to the esteemed rank of Captain.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
